## 3. Recommended AWS Architecture (Production)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> SQLite is **not suitable for production** under concurrent load. The migration to **RDS (PostgreSQL/MySQL)** is the single most critical infrastructure change.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Client Layer"
        APP["📱 Flutter Mobile App<br/>(Play Store / App Store)"]
    end

    subgraph "AWS Cloud"
        subgraph "Edge & Networking"
            R53["Route 53<br/>DNS"]
            CF["CloudFront<br/>CDN"]
            ALB["Application Load Balancer<br/>HTTPS :443"]
        end

        subgraph "Compute — ECS Fargate"
            ECS1["API Container 1<br/>Node.js"]
            ECS2["API Container 2<br/>Node.js"]
        end

        subgraph "Data Layer"
            RDS["RDS PostgreSQL<br/>Multi-AZ<br/>db.t3.micro"]
            S3["S3 Bucket<br/>Uploads / Logos"]
        end

        subgraph "Monitoring & Secrets"
            CW["CloudWatch<br/>Logs + Alarms"]
            SM["Secrets Manager<br/>DB Creds, API Keys"]
            ECR["ECR<br/>Docker Images"]
        end
    end

    APP -->|HTTPS| R53
    R53 --> ALB
    ALB --> ECS1
    ALB --> ECS2
    ECS1 --> RDS
    ECS2 --> RDS
    ECS1 --> S3
    ECS2 --> S3
    CF --> S3
    ECS1 -.->|logs| CW
    ECS2 -.->|logs| CW
    ECS1 -.->|secrets| SM
```

---

## 4. AWS Services Breakdown

### 4.1 Compute — ECS Fargate (Recommended)

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Service** | Amazon ECS (Fargate launch type) |
| **Why Fargate** | Serverless containers — no EC2 management, auto-scaling |
| **Image Registry** | Amazon ECR (Elastic Container Registry) |
| **Task Definition** | 0.5 vCPU, 1 GB RAM (start), auto-scale to 4 tasks |
| **Health Check** | `GET /api/health` → 200 OK |

**Dockerfile** (to be created at `backend/Dockerfile`):
```dockerfile
FROM node:20-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --only=production
COPY . .
RUN mkdir -p uploads
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["node", "server.js"]
```

> [!TIP]
> **Alternative (Budget)**: A single **EC2 t3.micro** with PM2 process manager is sufficient for < 100 concurrent users and falls under Free Tier.

### 4.2 Database — Amazon RDS

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Engine** | PostgreSQL 16 (or MySQL 8) |
| **Instance** | `db.t3.micro` (Free Tier eligible) |
| **Storage** | 20 GB gp3, auto-scaling to 100 GB |
| **Multi-AZ** | Enable for production (automatic failover) |
| **Backups** | Automated, 7-day retention |

> [!CAUTION]
> **Migration Required**: The current SQLite schema must be migrated to PostgreSQL. All `db.run()` / `db.get()` / `db.all()` calls in [server.js](file:///c:/Users/admin/Desktop/Time%20Tracker/backend/server.js) must be refactored to use a PostgreSQL driver (e.g., `pg` or `knex.js` ORM).

**Key Schema Tables to Migrate**:

| Table | Rows (est.) | Multi-Tenant Key |
|-------|------------|------------------|
| `users` | Primary | `company` column |
| `attendance` | High volume | via `userId` → `users.company` |
| `leaves` | Medium | via `userId` → `users.company` |
| `settings` | Low (1 per company) | `company` column |
| `holidays` | Low | `company` column (NULL = global) |
| `shifts` | Low | `company` column |
| `leave_policies` | Low | `company` column |
| `leave_balances` | Medium | via `userId` |
| `notifications` | High volume | via `userId` |
| `payslips` | Medium | `company` column |

### 4.3 File Storage — Amazon S3

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Bucket** | `time-tracker-uploads-{env}` |
| **Purpose** | Profile pictures, company logos, generated payslips |
| **Access** | Private, presigned URLs for read access |
| **CDN** | CloudFront distribution for fast global image delivery |
| **Lifecycle** | Move to S3 IA after 90 days, Glacier after 1 year |

**Code Changes Required**:
- Replace `multer` local disk storage with `multer-s3`
- Update `ApiService.getImageUrl()` in Flutter to use S3/CloudFront URLs
- Replace `/uploads/` static serving with S3 presigned URLs

### 4.4 Networking

| Component | Configuration |
|-----------|--------------|
| **VPC** | Custom VPC with 2 public + 2 private subnets (2 AZs) |
| **ALB** | Application Load Balancer in public subnets, HTTPS only |
| **Security Groups** | ALB: allow 443 inbound; ECS: allow 3000 from ALB only; RDS: allow 5432 from ECS only |
| **Route 53** | `api.timetracker.yourdomain.com` → ALB |
| **ACM** | SSL/TLS certificate for the domain |

### 4.5 Monitoring & Logging

| Service | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| **CloudWatch Logs** | Container stdout/stderr, API request logs |
| **CloudWatch Alarms** | CPU > 70%, Memory > 80%, 5xx error rate > 1% |
| **CloudWatch Dashboards** | API latency, request count, error rates |
| **SNS** | Alert notifications to team (email/Slack) |

### 4.6 Secrets Management

| Secret | Service |
|--------|---------|
| Database credentials | AWS Secrets Manager |
| API keys (future OTP/SMS) | AWS Secrets Manager |
| Environment config | ECS Task Definition environment variables |

