## 9. Migration Roadmap

```mermaid
gantt
    title AWS Migration Phases
    dateFormat  YYYY-MM-DD
    section Phase 1 - Foundation
    VPC & Networking Setup        :p1a, 2026-03-01, 2d
    RDS PostgreSQL Setup          :p1b, after p1a, 2d
    S3 Bucket + IAM Policies      :p1c, after p1a, 1d
    section Phase 2 - Code Changes
    SQLite → PostgreSQL Migration :p2a, after p1b, 5d
    Multer → S3 Upload Migration  :p2b, after p1c, 3d
    Add JWT Auth                  :p2c, after p2a, 3d
    Add Health Check Endpoint     :p2d, after p2a, 1d
    section Phase 3 - Containerize
    Create Dockerfile             :p3a, after p2d, 1d
    ECR Setup + Push Image        :p3b, after p3a, 1d
    ECS Fargate Service Setup     :p3c, after p3b, 2d
    section Phase 4 - Go Live
    ALB + Route 53 + SSL          :p4a, after p3c, 2d
    CI/CD Pipeline                :p4b, after p4a, 2d
    Staging Testing               :p4c, after p4b, 3d
    Production Cutover            :p4d, after p4c, 1d
    Monitoring & Alerting         :p4e, after p4d, 1d
```

| Phase | Duration | Description |
|-------|----------|-------------|
| **Phase 1** — Foundation | ~3 days | VPC, RDS, S3, IAM setup |
| **Phase 2** — Code Changes | ~8 days | DB migration, S3 uploads, JWT auth |
| **Phase 3** — Containerize | ~3 days | Dockerfile, ECR, ECS Fargate |
| **Phase 4** — Go Live | ~7 days | ALB, DNS, CI/CD, testing, cutover |
| **Total** | **~3 weeks** | End-to-end migration |

---

## 10. Critical Pre-Deployment Decisions

> [!WARNING]
> These decisions must be made by the engineering/product team before the DevOps engineer begins work.

1. **Database Engine**: PostgreSQL (recommended) or MySQL?
2. **Domain Name**: What will `api.{domain}` be?
3. **JWT vs Session Auth**: Implement JWT before deployment?
4. **OTP/SMS Provider**: Twilio, AWS SNS, or MSG91 for real OTP?
5. **Push Notifications**: Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) integration?
6. **Budget Tier**: Minimal ($40/mo) or Production ($118/mo)?
7. **Flutter API URL**: Hardcoded or runtime config (Firebase Remote Config)?

